---
import LegalPage from "../layouts/LegalPage.astro";

const title = "Security Policy · Donegal Airport";
const description = "Donegal Airport's Security Policy Statement, signed by the Chairman of the Board and the Managing Director (Accountable Manager).";
---

<LegalPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  eyebrow="Aerodrome"
  heading="Security Policy"
>
  <p>
    Donegal Airport's Security Policy aim is to achieve and maintain the highest levels of security
    within the aerodrome and its environs and to minimise security risks as far as is reasonably
    practicable.
  </p>
  <p>
    This Security Policy is signed by both the Chairman of the Board of Directors and the Managing
    Director of the Airport (Accountable Manager) and is displayed in all Functional Areas of the
    Aerodrome.
  </p>
  <p>
    Security is a high organisational priority that is mutually supportive of both commercial and
    operational priorities. Donegal Airport Management will support the management of security by
    creating a Security Culture that encourages security practices, effective security reporting
    and communication, and proactively and explicitly manages security through the application of
    a formal Security Management System.
  </p>
  <p>
    Donegal Airport will ensure sufficient resources are allocated to security in terms of both
    equipment which meets the regulatory standards, and ensuring that a sufficient number of
    Management and Staff are trained to a level of competency to be able to implement security
    strategies and processes. Management will also ensure staff are allocated only those tasks
    commensurate with their skills and competencies.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Chairman, on behalf of the Board of Directors, has overall responsibility for security
    within Donegal Airport. Security is an integral function of the organisation, and all staff
    have responsibility to ensure that security standards and best practices are implemented at
    all times.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Security Policy shall be reviewed periodically, and at least annually, by the Safety,
    Security &amp; Quality Committee.
  </p>
  <p>
    Donegal Airport is committed to implementing a continuous improvement programme in security
    and working at all times towards the highest security standards that, at a minimum, comply
    with the requirements of:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The National Civil Aviation Security Programme</li>
    <li>EU Regulations</li>
  </ul>
</LegalPage>
